---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const pageSlug = 'privacy';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Vireault privacy policy: no account, no vault data collection, offline local storage on your Android device."
  path="/privacy"
  pageSlug={pageSlug}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
    <article class="section prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="note">Last updated: 5 November 2026 (Europe/London)</p>
      <p>
        Vireault (“the app”, package <strong>{SITE.packageId}</strong>) is a local encrypted vault for Android.
        This policy describes what we do and do not collect.
      </p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, email or phone number is required.</li>
        <li>Vault contents stay on your device unless you export a backup file yourself.</li>
        <li>We do not operate a content server that receives your photos, videos, files, unlock secrets or encryption keys.</li>
        <li>We do not sell personal data.</li>
        <li>Purchases are processed by Google Play; Vireault does not receive your payment card details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data we do not collect</h2>
      <p>
        The app is designed for offline, local use. We do not collect vault files, thumbnails, file names, PINs, patterns,
        passphrases, master keys or backup recovery material. There is no analytics SDK in the product description used for this site,
        and the vault workflow does not depend on sending content to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Encrypted vault data, the encrypted index and unlock-related material needed to open your vaults are stored locally on your phone.
        Uninstalling the app or deleting a vault removes that local data from the app’s storage. If you created an encrypted backup file,
        that file remains wherever you saved it until you delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions and platform services</h2>
      <p>
        Access to photos or documents happens through the Android system pickers when you choose to import.
        Screenshot blocking and auto-lock are local protections. Google Play Billing handles subscriptions and the lifetime purchase;
        Google’s terms and privacy policy apply to payment processing.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Vireault is a utility app and is not directed at children under 13. Do not use it to store others’ private data without permission.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, we will update the date above on this page.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a></p>
    </article>
    <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} heading="Privacy-first by design" body="No account. Offline encryption on your Android phone." />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
